         (plant_versions note 17) x this plant's m.g.h ratio 76.1 / 62.2 N.m = 1.22 (both at the home keyframe;
         1.24 settled), rounded to 1.2, for the legs
         (hip pitch 150, roll 100, knee 180, ankle 100 on r4); tail servos x their own subtree gravity-torque ratio
         against r4's (60 / 50 / 50 / 40 -> 36 / 30 / 36 / 40), with tail_3 raised to 50 as the rod base; neck /
         head kp ~ 12 x tau_g (preload ~4.7 deg; no counterpart on r4, whose neck is welded); the claw
         5 N.m/rad, bounded at 4 N.m (~70 N at the tip).  forcerange 1.5 x kp on hip pitch, knee and ankle (gait
         headroom: 0.8 x kp clipped the r2 raptor's gait torque, docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md), 0.8 x kp on everything else.  Hip roll: 2 x (kp + k) = 288 N.m/rad against m.g.h
         76.1 (3.79 x; the T. rex's bar 1.5 x, note 13).  Home ctrl: the pose plus tau_g/kp on the neck, head and legs;
