  <sensor>
    <!-- 0-9 are the shared IMU block, which shared code indexes by POSITION (gyro 0-2, accel 3-5, quat 6-9):
             keep it first.  Touch sensors: one per LOAD-BEARING BODY (a touch sensor only sums contacts on
             geoms of its site's own body: notes 3 and 14d): r/l_foot = the MTP pad (metatarsus body) at 10/11,
             digits III and IV at 24-27.  Their sum equals the floor force on the six supports: digit II's
             phalanges are visual and its claw 2/2, so they never touch, and the MT shaft stays clear at and near
             the stance (exact on every live step at action noise 0.3, stance config, 100 seeds).  Only in a
             collapse does the shaft load the floor (at action noise 1.0, 2 of 18216 live steps of 300 seeds, at
             most 33 N), and the pad's channel then reads what of it falls inside the pad's touch site.
             head_tip 12-14 and tail tip 15-23 as the T. rex; claw tips 28-33: kept as the r4 raptor's
             claw telemetry (the env's claw reward reads site_xpos, so nothing consumes them).
             VelociraptorMongoliensisEnv._cache_ids resolves every sensor it reads BY NAME and fails closed on a
             missing one, so a reorder moves no observation channel; a rename or a new touch sensor needs its
             foot groups updated, and the plant contract fingerprints the foot channels by sensor name. -->
